{
 "gdd": "chart-table-web-map-and-menus",
 "blocking": [
  "Acceptance Criteria AC-CT-14 auto half (L1780) vs CT-45 (c), AC-CT-135 (c): [main review, confirmed by creative-director] The auto half expects the first NAV_DOWN after POINTER{MOVE} to move focus to the item below the retained control. CT-45 (c), the criterion's own half b (where ACCEPT_DOWN only reveals the bracket) and its manual half all say the first press only reveals the bracket on the retained focus. A correct implementation fails the auto half. An implementation that passes it moves an unseen focus, and a player who cannot see where focus is loses trust in the menu. FIX: Rewrite the auto half as two steps. First NAV_DOWN: the bracket is revealed on Y and focus stays Y. Second NAV_DOWN: focus moves to the item below Y. Keep 'no ui_* action'. Then align the 'reappears' wording in AC-CT-135, EC-CT-14 and CT-6.",
  "Detailed Rules CT-1 (L230), AC-CT-8 (L1772), Player Controller Interactions row (L592) vs player-controller-input.md L116: [main review, confirmed by creative-director] CT-1 still says the layer opens 'from the gameplay or inspect_card context (PCI:62: pause is reachable from both)'. The Controller owns input contexts, and its amendment at PCI L116 says 'chart_table is never entered from inspect_card': that press closes the card and nothing else. Under G1 the owner's rule stands, so AC-CT-8 cannot pass against the real Adapter. FIX: CT-1: open from gameplay only. Pressing in inspect_card closes the card and makes no kernel call; a second press opens the layer. Rewrite AC-CT-8 the same way, update the L592 row, CT-5 and the coverage matrix, and add *(Amended 2026-10-28 - cross-GDD fix, G1)* markers.",
  "Acceptance Criteria Glossary 'WM-36 list' (L1746) vs AC-CT-4 (L1768), CT-15, AC-CT-130: [main review, confirmed by creative-director] The glossary's field list is nodes[], pod_at, transit_state and destination_ready, with no leg_target_id or leg_dir. AC-CT-4 says every field read must be on that list, but CT-15 requires reading those two fields to draw the OUT-leg route. A correct implementation fails AC-CT-4. FIX: Add leg_target_id and leg_dir to the glossary list. Also state whether leg_origin_id is read (see the BACK-leg item). Re-state AC-CT-4 against the corrected list.",
  "ASK-CT-15 / ASK-CT-19 / C-10 / AC-CT-117, 118, 127 vs player-controller-input.md L118: [main review, confirmed by creative-director] The Controller has no MenuInput stream (0 occurrences), and PCI L118 still says the Chart Table 're-reads' the move_* axes and that 'accept is interact (E / LMB / A)'. That contradicts CT-45, AC-CT-117 (no ACCEPT from a mouse button) and the AC-CT-118 lint, which forbids reading devices. The GDD itself marks ASK-CT-15 BLOCKING before ADR (e). C-10 also cannot be met: with a CONFIRM_HOLD_S base above 1.5 s and HOLD_EFF_MAX_S = 1.9, the gap between the Delete hold and the confirm hold drops below 0.4 s. Creative-director weight: that failure lands exactly on players who use long accessibility holds, where the separation between Delete and Quit matters most. It is a player-safety issue, not a technicality. FIX: Under G6 the fix belongs in the owner, player-controller-input.md. Publish the MenuInput stream (NAV/ACCEPT down and up, BACK, CLOSE, FOCUS_OUT/IN, DEVICE_CHANGED, POINTER, plus echo suppression, hysteresis and the closing-control latch). Drop LMB from chart_table accept. Cap the Delete-paired hold base at 1.5 s (HOLD_EFF_MAX_S - 0.4). Then mark ASK-CT-15 and ASK-CT-19 answered in the Chart Table. Fallback if the owner declines: state it in ASK-CT-15 and scope C-10 / AC-CT-127 to bases of 1.5 s or less.",
  "AC-CT-137 (L1929), CT-21, TX-39, OQ-CT-37 vs save-load-and-versioned-format.md SAVE_QUIT_TIMEOUT_MS (L962) and L838: [main review, confirmed by creative-director] AC-CT-137 asserts FAILED within 3,000 ms and treats any configured value above 3,000 ms as a contract mismatch. Save/Load (the owner) still defaults SAVE_QUIT_TIMEOUT_MS to 5,000 ms and has no amendment for G2. The 'SaveDouble that never returns' setup also tests the double's script rather than the layer, because CT-21 forbids the layer from running its own watchdog. TX-39 depends on a 'window-close write in progress' signal that Save/Load does not publish, and quit_held has no consuming CT rule. FIX: Preferred under G6: in Save/Load, set the default to 3,000 ms, update AC-SL-45c, and publish a quit-write-in-progress read (or define it as save_status WRITING with kind QUIT). Give quit_held a consumer row in the Chart Table. Rewrite AC-CT-137 so the SaveDouble publishes FAILED at the configured timeout and the contract test asserts the owner's default is 3,000 ms or less. Alternative: conform to 5,000 ms and remove the 3,000 ms ceiling from CT-21."
 ]
}
